# less: TERM=vt100 (compiled-in ncurses fallback). Keys come from the console via
# fd 2 (open_tty falls back to fd 2: no /dev/tty node). The console is LINE mode
# (kernel echoes and returns on newline), so each key is followed by a newline,
# which less treats as "forward one line".
# -X keeps the screen. Page 1 shows lines 1..23; "G" jumps to the end;
# "?line 077" searches BACKWARD with the POSIX regex (a forward search from the
# end correctly says "Pattern not found"); "q" quits.
# NEGATIVE CONTROL xfail-less-nomatch: a pattern absent from the file must not be
# reported as found.
less-page|0|/bin/less|less|-X|/etc/lines.txt
@less-page|line 001 the first line
@less-page|line 023
@less-page|line 100 the last line
# the match is shown highlighted: ESC[7m line 077 ESC[m " searched"
@less-page|.\[7mline 077.\[m searched
less-pipe-mode|0|/bin/less|less|-F|-X|/etc/short.txt
@less-pipe-mode|short file line 1$
@less-pipe-mode|short file line 3
xfail-less-nomatch|0|/bin/less|less|-X|/etc/lines.txt
@xfail-less-nomatch|.\[7mline 077.\[m searched
!xfail-less-nomatch|Pattern not found
